---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LegalPage from "../../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, CONTACT_EMAIL_MAILTO, LEGAL_FREESTYLE_LAST_UPDATED, THIRD_PARTY_POLICY_URLS } from "../../constants";

const FREESTYLE_DELETE_ACCOUNT_PATH = "/freestyle-rap/delete-account";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Freestyle Rap" canonicalPath="/freestyle-rap/privacy">
  <LegalPage eyebrow="Freestyle Rap" themeColor="app-freestyle">
    <h1>Privacy Policy for Freestyle Rap</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {LEGAL_FREESTYLE_LAST_UPDATED}</p>

    <p>
      This privacy policy applies to the Freestyle Rap app (the &quot;Application&quot;) for mobile devices, provided by
      Lyricspiration and Khonsu Development (the &quot;Service Provider&quot;). The Application is supported by ads and
      is provided &quot;AS IS&quot;.
    </p>

    <h2>What information does the Application process and why?</h2>
    <h3>Information you provide</h3>
    <p>
      You can use most features of the Application without creating a Google account. If you contact the Service Provider
      (for example, by email), the Service Provider will process the information you provide in your message to
      respond to you.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you choose to sign in with Google, the Application processes information from your Google account (such as your
      email address and profile photo) to show your account in the app and to link purchases and preferences to your
      account.
    </p>

    <h3>Optional Google account, purchases, and cloud sync</h3>
    <p>
      Signing in with Google is optional for training features, but required before you can buy beats in the Beat Store.
      When you sign in, the Application links your Google account to a Firebase user profile and may store the following
      in Google Firebase (Firestore and Cloud Functions), associated with your Firebase user ID:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Purchase entitlements</strong>: which beats you have unlocked, and metadata needed to verify Google Play
        purchases and prevent duplicate grants (for example, purchase tokens and product IDs).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Favorite beats</strong>: the list of beat IDs you mark as favorites, so favorites can sync across your
        devices when you use the same Google account.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Payment card details are processed by Google Play, not by the Service Provider. The Service Provider does not
      receive your full payment credentials.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you sign out of Google in the Application, cloud sync for favorites stops. Favorites already stored on your
      device remain there. Purchase entitlements remain linked to your Google account and are available again when you
      sign back in with the same account.
    </p>

    <h3>Anonymous app session</h3>
    <p>
      The Application may sign you in anonymously to Firebase when you open it. This anonymous session helps deliver beat
      content and protect backend access (for example, via Firebase App Check). It is not the same as signing in with
      Google and does not by itself store your favorites or purchases in the cloud.
    </p>

    <h3>Information stored on your device</h3>
    <p>
      The Application stores certain data locally on your device, including freestyle recordings, app settings, cached
      beat files, favorite beats (when you are not signed in or before sync completes), and purchase state used for
      offline access. Recordings are not uploaded to the Service Provider&apos;s servers.
    </p>

    <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
    <p>
      The Application and its third-party service providers may process certain technical information automatically,
      such as device information (for example, device model, operating system version), IP address, app version,
      approximate location inferred from IP address, and identifiers associated with your device or app instance (for
      example, the advertising ID). This information is used to deliver ads, measure ad performance, improve stability,
      diagnose crashes, and understand how the Application is used.
    </p>
    <p>
      Firebase Analytics may receive usage events (for example, which screens you open and freestyle session settings
      such as beat, language, and speed). These events do not include your audio recordings.
    </p>

    <h2>Does the Application collect precise real-time location?</h2>
    <p>The Application does not collect precise real-time location information (for example, GPS location).</p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>The Application uses third-party services that have their own privacy policies. In particular:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href={THIRD_PARTY_POLICY_URLS.googleAdMob}>Google AdMob</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={THIRD_PARTY_POLICY_URLS.googlePrivacy}>Google</a> (Sign-In and account services)
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={THIRD_PARTY_POLICY_URLS.googlePlayTerms}>Google Play</a> (in-app purchases and billing)
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={THIRD_PARTY_POLICY_URLS.firebasePrivacy}>Firebase</a> (Analytics, Crashlytics, Authentication,
        Firestore, Cloud Functions, App Check, and Storage for beat assets)
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Legal bases (EEA/UK)</h2>
    <p>
      If you are located in the EEA or the UK, the Service Provider processes personal data under the following legal
      bases, depending on the purpose:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Consent</strong>: for ad-related identifiers and similar technologies where required, via Google&apos;s
        User Messaging Platform (UMP).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Contract</strong>: to provide beat purchases, restore entitlements, and sync favorites when you sign in
        with Google.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legitimate interests</strong>: to ensure security, prevent abuse, diagnose and fix crashes (for
        example, via Crashlytics), and understand aggregate app usage (for example, via Analytics).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal obligations</strong>: where processing is required to comply with applicable laws.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Consent management and opt-out</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Manage consent (EEA/UK)</strong>: if you are shown a consent prompt, you can typically review and update
        your choices in the Application&apos;s privacy settings (for example, a &quot;Manage consent&quot; option) where
        available.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Device controls</strong>: you can limit ad personalization via your device settings (for example,
        Android advertising settings).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google account</strong>: you can sign out in the Application&apos;s account settings. To delete your
        account and remove cloud data linked to it, follow the steps on our{" "}
        <a href={FREESTYLE_DELETE_ACCOUNT_PATH}>account deletion page</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Uninstall</strong>: you can stop further data processing by uninstalling the Application. Local data on
        the device is removed when the app is uninstalled.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      Crash, analytics, and ad measurement data are processed by the third-party services listed above and retained
      according to their retention settings and policies. Purchase and favorites data stored in Firebase is kept for as
      long as needed to provide the service and enforce entitlements, unless you request deletion or the Service Provider
      no longer needs it for legal or operational reasons. The Service Provider retains communications (if you contact
      them) for as long as needed to respond and for a reasonable period thereafter.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The Application is not intended for children and the Service Provider does not knowingly collect personal data
      from children. If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has provided personal information, contact
      the Service Provider at{" "}
      <a href={CONTACT_EMAIL_MAILTO}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      The Service Provider takes reasonable measures to protect information processed in connection with the
      Application. However, no method of transmission or storage is completely secure.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights such as access, rectification, deletion, objection, restriction,
      and portability. If the GDPR (or UK GDPR) applies, you also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory
      authority. To exercise your rights, including account deletion, see our{" "}
      <a href={FREESTYLE_DELETE_ACCOUNT_PATH}>account deletion page</a> or contact{" "}
      <a href={CONTACT_EMAIL_MAILTO}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      The third-party services used by the Application may process data on servers located in different countries. Where
      required, transfers are protected using appropriate safeguards, such as standard contractual clauses.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. The Service Provider will publish the updated policy on this
      page and update the &quot;Last updated&quot; date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about privacy while using the Application, contact the Service Provider at{" "}
      <a href={CONTACT_EMAIL_MAILTO}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
